1
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:07,080
[Fragments of Truth]

2
00:01:07,080 --> 00:01:08,600
[Episode 8]

3
00:01:18,920 --> 00:01:19,680
Are you Chen Yun?

4
00:01:19,840 --> 00:01:20,840
We're from the police station.

5
00:01:21,120 --> 00:01:22,640
Has your husband Wu Jia been back?

6
00:01:22,870 --> 00:01:23,430
He's not here.

7
00:01:27,120 --> 00:01:28,230
Do you know where he went?

8
00:01:29,710 --> 00:01:30,310
Baby.

9
00:01:30,640 --> 00:01:31,150
Baby.

10
00:02:24,710 --> 00:02:25,680
Is that your child?

11
00:02:34,710 --> 00:02:37,400
Is your child a boy or a girl?

12
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:44,030
The child's father.

13
00:02:44,910 --> 00:02:45,870
Do you know where he is too?

14
00:02:52,310 --> 00:02:53,280
Don't touch my child.

15
00:02:53,910 --> 00:02:54,680
Put the knife down!

16
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:10,680
Hey.

17
00:03:12,470 --> 00:03:12,800
Ms. Yun.

18
00:03:13,430 --> 00:03:14,080
Are you okay?

19
00:03:14,310 --> 00:03:14,960
Who are you?

20
00:03:16,800 --> 00:03:17,120
Oh.

21
00:03:17,470 --> 00:03:18,120
I'm Zhou Yong.

22
00:03:18,310 --> 00:03:19,120
I'm your downstairs neighbor.

23
00:03:19,910 --> 00:03:20,120
No.

24
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:21,150
Officers,

25
00:03:21,280 --> 00:03:22,030
what brings you here?

26
00:03:22,840 --> 00:03:23,080
Oh.

27
00:03:23,910 --> 00:03:24,840
We're just here to ask some questions.

28
00:03:24,840 --> 00:03:26,000
We need to understand the situation.

29
00:03:26,120 --> 00:03:26,910
We accidentally upset her.

30
00:03:27,240 --> 00:03:27,710
Nothing serious.

31
00:03:28,280 --> 00:03:28,680
Oh.

32
00:03:30,190 --> 00:03:30,470
Ah.

33
00:03:31,240 --> 00:03:32,080
Your hand's hurt?

34
00:03:32,910 --> 00:03:33,840
Let me see if you have any medicine.

35
00:03:34,710 --> 00:03:35,630
Where's the medicine?

36
00:03:39,400 --> 00:03:40,750
Hey, where is it?

37
00:03:42,470 --> 00:03:43,430
Couldn't find it.

38
00:03:43,430 --> 00:03:44,470
Maybe you should go to a hospital.

39
00:03:45,840 --> 00:03:46,710
It's fine. Just a scratch.

40
00:03:46,910 --> 00:03:47,470
A quick wash will do.

41
00:03:47,870 --> 00:03:48,120
Ah.

42
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:50,280
Ms. Yun.

43
00:03:50,710 --> 00:03:51,280
It's okay now.

44
00:03:51,470 --> 00:03:52,590
The police are here. Don't be afraid.

45
00:03:55,800 --> 00:03:56,680
You're Zhou Yong, right?

46
00:03:57,910 --> 00:03:58,190
Ah.

47
00:03:58,360 --> 00:03:58,750
Come here.

48
00:04:00,910 --> 00:04:01,280
Officer.

49
00:04:02,430 --> 00:04:03,280
Are you close to them?

50
00:04:03,910 --> 00:04:04,520
What about their family?

51
00:04:05,520 --> 00:04:06,280
Not really.

52
00:04:06,280 --> 00:04:06,910
Didn't I say that?

53
00:04:06,910 --> 00:04:07,910
I'm their downstairs neighbor.

54
00:04:08,800 --> 00:04:10,750
But Ms. Yun is getting worse.

55
00:04:11,120 --> 00:04:12,150
And she's often home alone.

56
00:04:13,120 --> 00:04:14,280
Yeah, that's tough.

57
00:04:15,080 --> 00:04:15,710
Usually,

58
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:17,480
I come help her when I'm free.

59
00:04:19,920 --> 00:04:21,870
How long's this been going on?

60
00:04:22,070 --> 00:04:22,680
What happened?

61
00:04:25,480 --> 00:04:26,560
She lost the baby.

62
00:04:26,830 --> 00:04:28,040
It was devastating for Ms. Yun.

63
00:04:29,680 --> 00:04:30,360
That's why

64
00:04:30,920 --> 00:04:31,750
she developed mental health problems.

65
00:04:35,190 --> 00:04:36,950
Is she always like this, or...

66
00:04:37,560 --> 00:04:37,920
Only sometimes.

67
00:04:38,390 --> 00:04:39,240
She's usually fine.

68
00:04:39,830 --> 00:04:40,390
Otherwise,

69
00:04:40,600 --> 00:04:41,720
she'd have been hospitalized long ago.

70
00:04:42,720 --> 00:04:43,390
But please

71
00:04:43,560 --> 00:04:45,560
never mention the baby around her.

72
00:04:45,870 --> 00:04:46,390
Otherwise,

73
00:04:47,240 --> 00:04:48,040
she'll be like this again.

74
00:04:48,600 --> 00:04:48,870
By the way.

75
00:04:49,160 --> 00:04:49,560
Officer.

76
00:04:50,040 --> 00:04:52,070
She's never hurt anyone before.

77
00:04:52,240 --> 00:04:53,390
You won't press charges, will you?

78
00:04:54,120 --> 00:04:54,560
No.

79
00:04:55,270 --> 00:04:57,480
I upset her by accident too.

80
00:04:57,480 --> 00:04:58,240
I share some responsibility.

81
00:05:00,680 --> 00:05:02,390
Wu Jia, you know him, right?

82
00:05:02,870 --> 00:05:03,070
Oh.

83
00:05:03,360 --> 00:05:04,240
Brother Wu?

84
00:05:04,680 --> 00:05:05,830
Seen him lately?

85
00:05:06,510 --> 00:05:07,430
Lately?

86
00:05:08,270 --> 00:05:09,720
Four or five days, maybe.

87
00:05:10,120 --> 00:05:11,510
I saw him downstairs once.

88
00:05:11,720 --> 00:05:13,040
But he didn't seem off.

89
00:05:14,310 --> 00:05:14,600
Okay.

90
00:05:15,600 --> 00:05:16,390
If you see him,

91
00:05:16,480 --> 00:05:17,120
let us know.

92
00:05:17,390 --> 00:05:17,920
Sure, don't worry.

93
00:05:17,920 --> 00:05:18,480
I'll fully cooperate.

94
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:18,920
Good, good.

95
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:19,120
Let's go.

96
00:05:19,870 --> 00:05:20,680
Sorry to trouble you both.

97
00:05:20,680 --> 00:05:21,430
No problem, no problem.

98
00:05:23,040 --> 00:05:23,750
Take care, officer.

99
00:05:34,680 --> 00:05:35,920
You head back. I'll look around.

100
00:05:36,160 --> 00:05:36,630
Mm.

101
00:05:53,920 --> 00:05:55,000
Ma'am, what are you looking at?

102
00:06:03,600 --> 00:06:04,720
Something's wrong with this building.

103
00:06:05,630 --> 00:06:06,870
A master told me

104
00:06:08,120 --> 00:06:09,310
that around this time today,

105
00:06:09,720 --> 00:06:10,830
the bad energy would peak.

106
00:06:12,870 --> 00:06:13,870
Nothing happened.

107
00:06:14,310 --> 00:06:15,870
That's only because you're lucky.

108
00:06:16,600 --> 00:06:16,950
Here.

109
00:06:26,120 --> 00:06:31,240
[Terrible Omen]

110
00:06:32,040 --> 00:06:32,510
Ma'am,

111
00:06:33,390 --> 00:06:34,800
you live next door to them.

112
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:36,680
Did you see Wu Jia?

113
00:06:40,070 --> 00:06:41,310
I can't really remember.

114
00:06:41,430 --> 00:06:43,600
I don't usually socialize.

115
00:06:44,310 --> 00:06:45,870
As for Wogua's family,

116
00:06:47,040 --> 00:06:47,870
I have no idea.

117
00:06:48,310 --> 00:06:50,040
Come on, young man. Have some water.

118
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:54,360
Auntie,

119
00:06:55,480 --> 00:06:58,240
what's wrong with this building?

120
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:00,600
Well...

121
00:07:01,390 --> 00:07:02,390
This house, well,

122
00:07:02,390 --> 00:07:03,480
it's really old.

123
00:07:04,190 --> 00:07:05,680
Many elderly residents died here.

124
00:07:06,680 --> 00:07:07,480
So the place already

125
00:07:08,680 --> 00:07:10,190
had a lot of negative energy.

126
00:07:10,870 --> 00:07:12,430
Then a few years ago,

127
00:07:12,870 --> 00:07:13,720
in the apartment next door,

128
00:07:14,750 --> 00:07:16,190
a baby died.

129
00:07:17,390 --> 00:07:18,310
Oh...

130
00:07:19,270 --> 00:07:20,720
Ever since then,

131
00:07:20,870 --> 00:07:23,800
this area has never been peaceful.

132
00:07:25,430 --> 00:07:28,270
Can you tell me what really happened?

133
00:07:28,630 --> 00:07:30,040
First came

134
00:07:30,870 --> 00:07:32,120
the demolition project
the year before last.

135
00:07:33,390 --> 00:07:36,430
A worker was crushed by a concrete slab.

136
00:07:38,190 --> 00:07:39,310
That very night,

137
00:07:40,360 --> 00:07:43,390
someone saw a child

138
00:07:43,920 --> 00:07:45,600
come to take the worker away.

139
00:07:46,560 --> 00:07:47,390
After that,

140
00:07:48,240 --> 00:07:51,120
the demolition project was abandoned.

141
00:07:52,070 --> 00:07:53,630
Later

142
00:07:54,120 --> 00:07:56,920
some reckless young people

143
00:07:58,070 --> 00:07:59,270
came here to film videos.

144
00:07:59,430 --> 00:08:00,480
No one knows

145
00:08:01,270 --> 00:08:02,480
what they saw.

146
00:08:02,480 --> 00:08:04,630
Two of them fainted on the spot.

147
00:08:04,720 --> 00:08:07,800
They even had to call an ambulance.

148
00:08:07,920 --> 00:08:12,270
You mean Chen Yun's miscarriage?

149
00:08:12,630 --> 00:08:13,160
Yeah.

150
00:08:13,630 --> 00:08:17,270
Then who else could it be?

151
00:08:17,720 --> 00:08:20,800
The baby died before it was born.

152
00:08:21,720 --> 00:08:24,160
It must harbor so much resentment.

153
00:08:24,680 --> 00:08:25,950
With them calling out to it,

154
00:08:26,040 --> 00:08:28,510
of course it came back for revenge.

155
00:08:28,510 --> 00:08:29,680
So you mean

156
00:08:31,120 --> 00:08:33,200
Wogua disappeared because of the fetus?

157
00:08:34,080 --> 00:08:35,240
Ouch.

158
00:08:35,600 --> 00:08:37,120
What a tragedy.

159
00:08:38,510 --> 00:08:38,960
Oh, what a tragedy.

160
00:08:38,960 --> 00:08:40,440
Such a tragedy.

161
00:08:41,320 --> 00:08:42,000
Ouch.

162
00:08:45,790 --> 00:08:46,240
Take a look.

163
00:08:46,240 --> 00:08:47,150
See how efficiently we work?

164
00:08:48,320 --> 00:08:48,630
Xiao Zhang.

165
00:08:48,720 --> 00:08:49,910
Yes, Officer Han?

166
00:08:50,120 --> 00:08:51,080
You're done asking, right?

167
00:08:51,200 --> 00:08:51,480
Yeah.

168
00:08:52,150 --> 00:08:52,720
About Lao Li...

169
00:08:52,720 --> 00:08:53,030
Yeah?

170
00:08:53,120 --> 00:08:55,480
Who is the old woman next to Chen Yun?

171
00:08:55,480 --> 00:08:56,000
Oh no.

172
00:08:56,720 --> 00:08:58,150
Mrs. Song.

173
00:08:58,480 --> 00:09:00,080
She lives alone.

174
00:09:00,200 --> 00:09:01,790
She survives by collecting scrap.

175
00:09:01,790 --> 00:09:02,870
She's a little eccentric.

176
00:09:03,670 --> 00:09:04,270
Just leave her alone.

177
00:09:05,120 --> 00:09:05,480
Okay.

178
00:09:06,320 --> 00:09:07,320
Do we have cameras here?

179
00:09:08,080 --> 00:09:08,960
Only at the two gates.

180
00:09:13,870 --> 00:09:14,390
That works.

181
00:09:14,870 --> 00:09:15,510
Copy it for me.

182
00:09:15,510 --> 00:09:16,510
The past week.

183
00:09:16,870 --> 00:09:17,600
Oh.

184
00:09:17,600 --> 00:09:18,440
One...

185
00:09:18,510 --> 00:09:19,390
A week.

186
00:09:19,550 --> 00:09:20,000
Okay.

187
00:09:20,720 --> 00:09:21,320
Oh no.

188
00:09:21,510 --> 00:09:22,440
Have a seat.

189
00:09:23,120 --> 00:09:23,870
It's fine, I'll look.

190
00:10:01,630 --> 00:10:02,200
Uncle He.

191
00:10:27,440 --> 00:10:28,550
Where were you all afternoon?

192
00:10:28,910 --> 00:10:30,320
Did the station visit take that long?

193
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:34,870
Take a look at this.

194
00:10:36,480 --> 00:10:37,630
This man is Wu Jia.

195
00:10:38,270 --> 00:10:39,320
He committed a crime seven years ago

196
00:10:39,320 --> 00:10:40,080
and was arrested.

197
00:10:40,510 --> 00:10:42,870
The crime occurred at Night Flight Club.

198
00:10:45,120 --> 00:10:46,120
I remember this guy.

199
00:10:46,720 --> 00:10:49,480
But that alone proves no connection.

200
00:10:50,390 --> 00:10:51,150
Look at this one too.

201
00:10:51,870 --> 00:10:52,790
This is his statement.

202
00:10:54,200 --> 00:10:54,910
Back then,

203
00:10:54,910 --> 00:10:56,510
to seek leniency,

204
00:10:56,790 --> 00:10:59,440
he confessed to crimes
involving Xu Haodong.

205
00:11:00,510 --> 00:11:01,320
It was very detailed.

206
00:11:01,320 --> 00:11:03,270
I think he knew Xu Haodong well.

207
00:11:04,720 --> 00:11:05,790
So you're saying

208
00:11:06,630 --> 00:11:08,120
he knew inside information
about Night Flight Club.

209
00:11:08,910 --> 00:11:09,240
Yes.

210
00:11:09,750 --> 00:11:11,120
So I looked into it.

211
00:11:11,320 --> 00:11:11,960
It's possible.

212
00:11:12,670 --> 00:11:13,120
Mm.

213
00:11:16,840 --> 00:11:17,550
You looked into it?

214
00:11:18,270 --> 00:11:18,510
Oh.

215
00:11:18,910 --> 00:11:19,550
Who authorized you?

216
00:11:23,440 --> 00:11:24,200
That was reckless.

217
00:11:25,840 --> 00:11:26,670
On a matter this serious,

218
00:11:26,790 --> 00:11:27,600
you acted alone.

219
00:11:27,870 --> 00:11:28,240
Ah.

220
00:11:28,790 --> 00:11:31,150
From Yu Hongfei to Wu Jia,

221
00:11:31,630 --> 00:11:32,870
they're disappearing one by one.

222
00:11:33,270 --> 00:11:33,960
Is that just a coincidence?

223
00:11:37,720 --> 00:11:38,240
Not sure.

224
00:11:39,320 --> 00:11:40,240
Han Ning,

225
00:11:40,440 --> 00:11:42,320
I don't know what to say to you.

226
00:11:45,270 --> 00:11:46,240
You graduated from Police University,

227
00:11:46,630 --> 00:11:48,320
yet showed no common sense.

228
00:11:48,630 --> 00:11:48,910
Ah.

229
00:11:52,030 --> 00:11:52,510
Think about it.

230
00:11:53,150 --> 00:11:55,670
If your investigation exposed
the mastermind,

231
00:11:56,120 --> 00:11:56,870
what could happen?

232
00:12:00,670 --> 00:12:01,120
Uncle He.

233
00:12:01,550 --> 00:12:02,000
Sorry.

234
00:12:03,200 --> 00:12:03,960
Sorry won't cut it.

235
00:12:05,910 --> 00:12:06,390
Well then,

236
00:12:06,750 --> 00:12:07,910
I'll report to the captain.

237
00:12:26,510 --> 00:12:27,200
Zero-One, Zero-One.

238
00:12:27,390 --> 00:12:28,120
Do you copy? Respond.

239
00:12:28,390 --> 00:12:29,440
Report your status.

240
00:12:30,910 --> 00:12:32,630
Zero-One, copy.

241
00:12:33,030 --> 00:12:34,390
I'm tracking the suspect.

242
00:13:07,030 --> 00:13:07,390
Over there.

243
00:13:59,570 --> 00:14:01,630
♪I stand in a fire-tempered jungle♪

244
00:14:01,630 --> 00:14:03,570
♪Withered leaves fall
as my strength runs dry♪

245
00:14:03,570 --> 00:14:05,480
♪Dust swirls as I clench my fists♪

246
00:14:05,480 --> 00:14:07,290
♪I strategize, my faith my armor♪

247
00:14:07,290 --> 00:14:09,630
♪My defiance spills onto concrete♪

248
00:14:09,630 --> 00:14:12,050
♪Even thick fog can't hide
my clear gaze♪

249
00:14:15,200 --> 00:14:17,100
♪Let neon turn to thorns♪

250
00:14:17,100 --> 00:14:19,000
♪Flying low as the stars shift and turn♪

251
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:20,950
♪Escape the maze,
transcend the challenge♪

252
00:14:20,950 --> 00:14:23,070
♪The meter starts, breaking the silence♪

253
00:14:23,100 --> 00:14:25,080
♪A beam cuts through
a crack in the wall♪

254
00:14:25,080 --> 00:14:27,240
♪This rhythm and noise
echo through the streets♪

255
00:14:30,840 --> 00:14:34,320
♪Don't be afraid. No one will answer♪

256
00:14:34,320 --> 00:14:37,680
♪Why is that child crying?♪

257
00:14:37,920 --> 00:14:40,390
♪The shrinking scar on my arm♪

258
00:14:40,390 --> 00:14:42,000
♪Means I've grown up♪

259
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:45,150
♪You can trust me when I say that♪

260
00:14:45,150 --> 00:14:48,640
♪The wound still aches♪

261
00:14:49,040 --> 00:14:53,400
♪Like a biting winter♪

262
00:14:53,400 --> 00:14:56,660
♪But a spark still glows♪

